This section covers the preparation of historical location data before importing it into QGIS.

1) Create a spreadsheet

Create a spreadsheet containing the locations to be mapped, including a unique name for each data point. The 'Name' column will later become the label for the point on the map. 

2) Add geographic coordinates

Each location needs geographic coordinates before it can be displayed as a point on the map.

Add separate columns for longitude and latitude:

![Excel spreadsheet containing the location data](../images/excel-data.png)

4) Save the spreadsheet

Save the spreadsheet as a standard Excel file and as a csv file. Keep the Excel file as the master copy of the dataset. If you need to add or remove locations in the future, make the changes in the Excel file and then save an updated CSV file, replacing the existing CSV.

The CSV file is the version used by QGIS. After updating it, reload the layer in QGIS to display the changes.

